From 1321f60033b2a6c7fd7474d4c034e61d18246223 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuya Hamamachi <yuya.hamamachi.sx@renesas.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:17:33 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: rppx1: imx477: Add LSC tuning

Convert the ALSC tables of the Raspberry Pi VC4 tuning file for the
imx477 to the format of the RPP-X1 lens shading correction and add them
to the imx477 tuning file.

The VC4 16x12 luminance table is mixed with the luminance_strength and
multiplied by the Cr/Cb calibration tables for each colour temperature
(2960K, 4850K and 5930K). The result is resampled to the 17x17 points of
the RPP-X1 table, and normalized per channel so that the minimum gain is
1.0 (1024 in the u2.10 fixed point).

Applying the same conversion to the imx708 VC4 file reproduces the
tables of imx708.yaml with a mean error of 0.2%.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Yuya Hamamachi <yuya.hamamachi.sx@renesas.com>
---
